message: "If you use or discuss this work, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Ramanujan, Landen, and Baker N-Series Refinement: Higher-Degree Modular Gap Laws and a Two-Axis Comparison"
type: article
authors:
  - family-names: Baker
    given-names: Wayne
date-released: 2026-07-13
version: preprint-v1
repository-code: "https://github.com/CWBaker360/ramanujan-landen-nseries-refinement"
url: "https://github.com/CWBaker360/ramanujan-landen-nseries-refinement"
abstract: >-
  This paper compares Ramanujan ellipse approximation, fixed N-series
  resolution cancellation, and Landen modular gap contraction. It proves the
  first-correction law delta(q^m)/delta(q)^m = 4^(1-m)(1 + 4m q^2 + O(q^4))
  for every fixed integer m at least two, derives the AGM linkage constant
  alpha_n/delta_n^2 tending to one eighth, and gives a guarded comparison with
  a companion cubic trisection error cascade.
keywords:
  - Ramanujan approximation
  - Landen transformation
  - elliptic nome
  - modular lambda function
  - arithmetic-geometric mean
  - N-series
  - asymptotic analysis
  - numerical verification
